From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAESink: a buffer with nothing to write still reports
 the sink delay

When ActiveAE corrects a stream that is behind, it skips samples out of
the front buffer, or drops a whole frame in passthrough, and can leave
that buffer empty. The empty buffer still goes to the sink.
OutputSamples() writes nothing for it and returns a delay it never read:
zero. The sink sets its next timeout to half the returned delay, times
out at once, and fills the gap with a buffer of silence - 50 ms of PCM,
one pause burst in passthrough. The skip is put straight back as a cut,
and the engine, which has already declared the stream in sync, finds it
that far behind again a second later, so the player steps the clock.
It happens whenever the next buffer has not reached the sink yet, which
on an Amlogic box was every third or fourth correction of a stream that
started behind after a seek. In passthrough the zero delay is also
published to the engine's stats as the sink delay.

Read the delay before writing, so an empty buffer reports the sink as
it is.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp
index 032e8f24..bc17d0ad 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp
@@ -1199,15 +1199,14 @@ unsigned int CActiveAESink::OutputSamples(CSampleBuffer* samples)
       m_stats->UpdateSinkDelay(status, samples->pool ? written : 0);
   }
 
+  // A packet dropped for a/v sync has no frames and never enters the loop above. Query the
+  // sink anyway, otherwise the engine is told the sink holds no audio at all and the next
+  // sync error measurements are off by the whole sink delay.
+  if (totalFrames == 0)
+    m_sink->GetDelay(status);
+
   if (m_requestedFormat.m_dataFormat == AE_FMT_RAW)
-  {
-    // A packet dropped for a/v sync has no frames and never enters the loop above. Query the
-    // sink anyway, otherwise the engine is told the sink holds no audio at all and the next
-    // sync error measurements are off by the whole sink delay.
-    if (!m_needIecPack && totalFrames == 0)
-      m_sink->GetDelay(status);
     m_stats->UpdateSinkDelay(status, samples->pool ? 1 : 0);
-  }
 
   return status.delay * 1000;
 }
